      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested**\n\nReturning the raw `rts_fp_return_t` code in the `default` case can leak vendor-specific positive integers (e.g., `RTS_FP_POOR_QUALITY \u003d 6`) or unmapped vendor negatives directly up to the caller. The Zephyr/Cros EC fingerprint API expects standard negative error codes (like `-EIO` or `-EINVAL`) for failures.\n\nPlease explicitly handle `RTS_FP_SUCCESS` (to return 0) and map all other unhandled vendor errors to a standard negative error code:\n\n```c\nstatic int convert_rts_get_image_error_code(rts_fp_return_t code)\n{\n\tswitch (code) {\n\tcase RTS_FP_SUCCESS:\n\t\treturn 0;\n\tcase RTS_ERROR_FAST_FINGER_UP:\n\t\treturn FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_SCAN_TOO_FAST;\n\tcase RTS_ERROR_IMAGE_PARTIAL:\n\t\treturn FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_SCAN_LOW_SENSOR_COVERAGE;\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn -EIO;\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/fb64d767-657a-4435-8092-5997823e25c3)",
